{
  "_doc": "Drafts the Outbox holds (shared/src/outbox-drafts.ts, Android :core OutboxDrafts.kt). A scheduled send stays a Gmail draft until it goes, but shows only in the Outbox. `drafts` are Gmail's (drafts.list) as {draftId, messageId, threadId}; `docs` the outbox docs as {draftId, status}. outboxDrafts(drafts, docs, sending, listedFor): every doc but a `sent` one holds its draft; `messageIds` are those drafts' message ids, `threadIds` the threads with no draft but those (sorted here). `count` is draftThreadCount(labelThreads, outbox): the DRAFT label's thread count less threadIds' size, never below 0. `listed` cases: onlyInOutbox(threadId, sentOrReceived, outboxDrafts(drafts, docs)) is true when the thread has no sent or received message and every draft in it is held, so it shows in no view but the Outbox (search included). `sending` (absent: none) are the drafts this device is sending, queued or with a doc just written, as {draftId, messageId, threadId} (any may be null); they hold their draft too, and their messageId is hidden. Gmail's listing lags, so `listedFor` (absent: none) is the drafts the Outbox held when `drafts` was listed: a held draft the listing leaves out and wasn't made for is newer than it and leaves Drafts by the threadId its sending entry or doc (`docs` may carry threadId) names, unless that thread has a draft not held; one the listing was made for and left out is gone and hides nothing. A sending entry with no draftId isn't in Gmail yet and hides no thread.",
